  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the application**\n\nI\'m now focusing on modularity, aiming for a cleaner `/src/App.tsx`. I want to build a robust foundation before tackling styling and interactivity. I\'m exploring how to best structure the application to keep `/src/App.tsx` compact and easy to maintain.\n\n\n**Defining the Components**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the product data and separate components into their own files to improve modularity. I\'m taking the user requests for the Navbar and Hero sections into account, and breaking down their requirements into distinct, manageable parts. The goal is to build these components in isolation. I\'m focusing on the Navbar now, planning the layout, logo details, and navigation menu, including the search and cart icons with their respective interactive features. I also began conceptualizing how the Hero section will introduce the product via a compelling \"Biotecnolog\303\255a\" banner.\n\n\n**Designing the Product Display**\n\nI\'m now diving into the product section. I\'m visualizing a grid of product cards with stunning Unsplash imagery \342\200\223 thinking high-fashion, minimalist shots in elegant colors. Each card will have the product name, price, and a brief tech description. I\'m focusing on an interactive shade selector with Earth/Nude tone circles. Clicking one should immediately update the card\'s displayed shade. Also, I plan an \"A\303\261adir al carrito\" button with `motion` animation.\n\n\n\n**Adding Interactive Features**\n\nI am now focusing on interactive elements, incorporating premium size recommendations, aesthetic social media icons (Instagram, Facebook, TikTok), and visual payment method mentions (Visa, MasterCard, AmEx). I\'m planning active visual states with the Cherry Rose color (#a4133c) for clicked buttons and links. I will also build an active cart drawer that supports removing items, changing quantities, and a promotional discount code box (\"ECLATVIP\" for 15% off). Finally, I\'m developing a registration/membership popup modal (\"Registro / Unirse\") for \303\211clat Club, which will provide free size consultation and priority releases. I will structure the files by putting types in `/src/types.ts` and mock products with high-fidelity imagery in `/src/data.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining Product Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on product-specific details. I want to generate attractive names like \"\303\211clat Sculpting Bodysuit\" and write rich descriptions centered on nanotechnology and compression. I\'m also preparing for the nude shade codes. I\'m actively structuring the `/src/components` to support these new details: Navbar, Hero, ProductGrid, ProductCard, VipModal, and RegisterModal.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/types.ts` to represent the models, products, colors, and cart states, laying a solid and type-safe architecture for the interactive mockup."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 547580982
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
